#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:5
#: a6c43d209f63409586690f327598d2bd
msgid "Funding Committee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:7
#: e7e632b507c74a9d90bb4129156b7c2f
msgid "ArduPilot collects funds through donations from :ref:`individuals <common-donation>` and `Partners <https://ardupilot.org/about/Partners>`__ and these are held within SPI and the ArduPilot Foundation. Some of these funds go to pay for fixed costs including servers (i.e. build servers, wiki servers, etc) and are billed directly to ArduPilot's account within SPI. Other project expenses and support engineer compensation is paid from the ArduPilot Foundation account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:10
#: 695b23b0f74a4bccb6bc2b6889cae706
msgid "The rules governing the Fundinng committee are setforth here: `Funding Committee Rules <https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l6M5fxjoLEv4TQYzvZhbcBYsUlxJOXSIEfELrACp6f8/edit?usp=sharing>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:12
#: 6f77611b15ce4af39574e1f3096fd03b
msgid "Each month SPI publishes an in-month and year-to-date financial report on the Treasurer `page <https://spi-inc.org/treasurer/>`__.  Annual Reports, containing a high level summary, are published `here <https://spi-inc.org/corporate/annual-reports/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:14
#: 4c0e1743938a4d9ea5c8e273581080e4
msgid "This page attempts to outline how ArduPilot Project funds are managed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:17
#: 9ffe12015769458c931050ed39794d76
msgid "Submitting Proposals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:19
#: d48ba71a4aa041ac9d96b6f0f65f086e
msgid "Anyone may submit a proposal to receive funding by opening a new topic within the `Discuss Forum's Proposal category <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/proposals>`__. Suggestions for what the proposal should include are described `here <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/about-the-funding-proposals-category/12255>`__ and also copied below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:22
#: 70a1b8c8c71943b98be728558f6835f4
msgid "Proposals should be no more than 2 pages and include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:24
#: 33e358b83cee40b8b595f1cfbd26fb57
msgid "description of the project and how it would improve ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:25
#: 59c5b55037e044fea56cce4a76f182bd
msgid "how much money is needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:26
#: cb998ac9a3ec4c73a8b946c25aa87875
msgid "what resources are needed (hardware, software, time)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:27
#: 4ea93a3be8f9464f8655400a7e543b91
msgid "what core developer support is required (if any)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:28
#: 096cb906ce5a4249a75f3268671fa1e8
msgid "timespan for the completion of the project (and milestones if longer than 3 months)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:29
#: 178299c14ab543e7b45d569303f21b93
msgid "what skills the developer has to complete the task (i.e. past experience contributing to ArduPilot)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:31
#: 35d25d0e77044204aceb642a75c2878d
msgid "All proposal submissions are considered public information, and may be disclosed to whatever audience is relevant at the time, such as developer or partner meetings and group calls, and may be published on the website or forums."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:33
#: 23aa0e26400c4da0b71827b88e193f9c
msgid "After posting the proposal, ping the Funding Committee in the dev-team-funding channel on Discord with a link to the proposal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:36
#: 8b1aea8fcf9f4abca097119decf00c93
msgid "Evaluating Proposals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:38
#: 974741cc97504b0183641e5c91b1537e
msgid "The ArduPilot funding committee is made up of three elected members from the team with elections held each December.  The currently elected members are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:40
#: 39fbe7302dca4fada3d5100a403b1b1c
msgid "Andrew Tridgell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:41
#: ce77f93308004d9295fa2b3d2fda2a16
msgid "James Pattison"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:42
#: 9762920e06e94383b20967065abc4d40
msgid "Andy Piper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:44
#: b01b8895947c4e5e96ed5c8e6f97b869
msgid "This committee reviews the `Proposal category <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/proposals>`__ regularly and evaluates proposals based on both the benefit to ArduPilot and likelihood of success. The approve/reject decision is made by a simple majority vote (i.e. 2 of 3 must approve)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:47
#: 5266da64362045be9b4da4f6ad058ea1
msgid "The committee has authority to decide on its own for funding requests up to $2000.  Above this, if the funding committee approves of the request, a member of the funding committee should raise a vote for the wider dev team to decide on the proposal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:49
#: 84b02c508df34c199999be76e54e3cbb
msgid "Additional guidance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:51
#: f4dcfa4056f543c48a8190580ae3b6f4
msgid "requests for small amounts of funding (eg. $200 to buy a new sensor) generally have a very low threshold for funding. Larger requests receive more scrutiny."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:52
#: f3099b441cef48cf91029d844aa1336c
msgid "for larger requests (i.e. over $2000) the committee may ask the applicant to undertake a smaller sub-task first to demonstrate their ability to take on the larger task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:53
#: fdc97c60f3264cf4b1ca197cc8a6542a
msgid "specific proposals are favored over less specific ones. For example, a proposal to “improve ArduPilot” would be less likely to be funded compared with a proposal to “add support for the XYZ gyroscope”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:54
#: 049c7d01116b46c2a2dd95712813b218
msgid "we should keep red-tape to a minimum. There is no point in there being 10 hours of admin for a $200 request. Small proposals should be encouraged which are just a few paragraphs, and the person should get their money quickly and with a minimum of fuss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:55
#: dd13d103014643bc856b71bfd1efd82f
msgid "all proposals should receive and accepted or rejected response within a reasonable amount of time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:58
#: f28bf0b09b6d4d1f89b69763c127c6ad
msgid "Getting Paid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:60
#: a5d9e18b14a74e9889fcc6eada36ae81
msgid "Payments from ArduPilot are made via PayPal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:62
#: 935722ffc4eb4961b16394410f4f2bbb
msgid "Email the receipts to funding@ardupilot.org, with a clear subject title linking it back to the original funding proposal. In the case of multiple receipts, collate them into a single email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:63
#: b3ec09b6abda41ae857391a185d969a2
msgid "Send a request for funds to ardupilot.devel@gmail.com. The request description must have a clear reference back to the original funding proposal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/how-the-team-works-development-fund.rst:64
#: 0cf3412982204151b54ee925aa676030
msgid "Again ping the Funding Committee in the dev-team-funding channel on Discord to ask if they can check the PayPal account and push the \"send funds\" button"
msgstr ""
